Locate — Find File using the OS locate command
================================================

Adds a "Find File" menu item to the Tools menu backed by the `locate`
command.  Searches are scoped to the open project root.

Result UX:
  0 matches  — dialog stays open for query refinement
  1 match    — path shown in dialog; press Enter to open
  2+ matches — clickable links in the Messages tab; dialog closes

A "updatedb" menu item runs `sudo updatedb` in the background (uses the
geanycli terminal tab if available).

Double-tap Shift opens the Find File dialog from anywhere in Geany.

Requirements
------------

mlocate or plocate must be installed on the system.

Known Issues
------------

None currently known.

